{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Clock","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Clock"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"GnustoClock"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11GnustoClock0B0V"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"derived, not ticked","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"now","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a pure function of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" counter, which means every rule, action, fuse and daemon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a turn reads the same time — including the timer tick at the end of it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A clock advanced by its own daemon would instead be read differently by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"daemons sorting before and after it in the tick order, making the time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depend on other timers’ ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"names","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". Deriving also inherits the engine’s notion","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of world time for free: the clock already doesn’t move on a parse error or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a meta command, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"take all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already costs one turn, not four.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let clock = Clock(startingAt: TimeOfDay(17, 30), minutesPerTurn: 2)","","var content: GameContents { clock }        \/\/ registers the verb and the state","var timers: [TimedEvent] {","    clock.at(TimeOfDay(17, 46), named: \"blast\") {","        say(\"The carriage house goes up with a sound like a door slamming in a cave.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now"},{"text":" needs a live turn, so it belongs in rule bodies, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"describe"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"blocks and actions — not in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" block, which is evaluated at bootstrap.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not provided: "},{"code":"wait until <time>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The parser has no numeric slot and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requires every token to be consumed, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wait until 8 15"},{"text":" can never match a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pattern; and jumping the clock inside one turn would run a single timer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tick, silently skipping any alarm in between. Waiting a named number of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turns is the honest version, and the engine already does it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"h